            <ArticleTitle>Circumferential craniocervical extradural tuberculous granulations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>808-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2009.07.120</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 49-year-old female presented with a 7-month history of progressive quadriparesis. Investigations revealed a circumferential lesion involving the cervicomedullary junction and the upper cervical cord. The firm extradural granulomatous lesion was partially resected. Histological examination revealed that the lesion comprised tuberculous granulation tissue, which resolved on anti-tuberculous drug treatment. We were unable to find a similar report of extradural tuberculous granuloma in our literature search.</AbstractText>
